.TH "dotnet-package-download" "1" "2025-12-29" "" ".NET Documentation"
.hy
.SH dotnet package download
.RS
.PP
Applies to: \[u2714]\[uFE0F] .NET 10.0.2xx SDK and later versions.
.RE
.SH NAME
.PP
dotnet-package-download \[em] Download one or more NuGet packages to disk.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet package download [<packages>...]
    [--output <path>]
    [--configfile <path> ]
    [--prerelease]
    [--source <package source>]
    [--allow-insecure-connections]
    [--interactive]
    [--verbosity <level>]

dotnet package download -h|--help
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[V]dotnet package download\f[R] downloads NuGet packages to a local directory.
It \f[B]does not\f[R] add or update \f[V]PackageReference\f[R] entries in project files and \f[B]does not\f[R] build or restore a project.
By default, the command downloads only the packages you specify (no transitive dependencies) to the current working directory.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]packages\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
One or more package IDs to download.
Each package can optionally include a version with \f[V]\[at]\f[R].
If a package version isn\[cq]t specified, the latest version of the package is downloaded.
For example, \f[V]dotnet package download Contoso.Utilities\f[R] or \f[V]dotnet package download Contoso.Utilities\[at]3.2.1\f[R].
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--allow-insecure-connections\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Allows downloading from HTTP sources.
Without this flag, insecure sources cause the command to error per HTTPS-everywhere (https://aka.ms/nuget-https-everywhere) guidance.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--configfile <path>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Path to a NuGet.config to use.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\f[VB]--interactive\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Allows the command to stop and wait for user input or action.
For example, to complete authentication.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]-o, --output <path>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Directory where the package will be placed.
Defaults to the current working directory.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--prerelease\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Allows downloading prerelease versions.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]-s --source <package source>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Specifies the NuGet package source to use.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\f[VB]-v|--verbosity <LEVEL>\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Sets the verbosity level of the command.
Allowed values are \f[V]q[uiet]\f[R], \f[V]m[inimal]\f[R], \f[V]n[ormal]\f[R], \f[V]d[etailed]\f[R], and \f[V]diag[nostic]\f[R].
For more information, see <xref:Microsoft.Build.Framework.LoggerVerbosity>.
.PP
\f[B]\f[VB]-?|-h|--help\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Prints out a description of how to use the command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Download a single package at a specific version
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet package download Contoso\[at]13.0.3 --output My/Destination/For/packages
\f[R]
.fi
.SS Download multiple packages to a custom folder
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet package download Contoso\[at]3.1.2 Contoso.Utility\[at]6.12.0 --output My/Destination/For/packages
\f[R]
.fi
